562
00:28:02,208 --> 00:28:04,750
We owe each other. Drop it.

563
00:28:04,833 --> 00:28:06,375
Eat. Quit yapping.

564
00:28:06,458 --> 00:28:07,666
A-Lan.

565
00:28:14,833 --> 00:28:15,666
Want one?

566
00:28:27,583 --> 00:28:28,833
You want some?

567
00:28:38,041 --> 00:28:39,208
Sorry.

568
00:28:44,958 --> 00:28:46,083
Thanks.

569
00:28:49,583 --> 00:28:50,750
I'm sorry too.

570
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:04,583
Make up.

571
00:29:06,333 --> 00:29:08,000
Give her a hug.

572
00:29:10,250 --> 00:29:11,291
Come on.

573
00:29:17,708 --> 00:29:20,083
Grandma, why doesn't she have to?

574
00:29:20,166 --> 00:29:21,000
Yeah.

575
00:29:21,083 --> 00:29:21,916
A-Pei.

576
00:29:23,875 --> 00:29:24,875
Me too.

577
00:29:25,416 --> 00:29:26,375
Okay.

578
00:29:26,458 --> 00:29:27,833
It's just a hug.

579
00:29:27,916 --> 00:29:29,208
Come on, come on.

580
00:29:29,291 --> 00:29:30,708
Don't be shy.

581
00:29:32,416 --> 00:29:34,375
Okay, it's fine.

582
00:29:35,083 --> 00:29:37,416
If it's good, eat a few more.

583
00:29:40,458 --> 00:29:42,166
Sorry…

584
00:29:43,500 --> 00:29:44,458
about what happened.

585
00:29:47,375 --> 00:29:48,333
All right.

586
00:29:48,416 --> 00:29:50,333
Have some cake.

587
00:29:50,416 --> 00:29:52,708
Let's eat.

588
00:29:54,166 --> 00:29:55,333
Yummy, yummy.

589
00:29:55,833 --> 00:29:56,958
Sis, here's a piece.

590
00:29:57,041 --> 00:29:57,875
Okay.

591
00:29:58,583 --> 00:29:59,750
Here.

592
00:30:00,875 --> 00:30:03,250
Look at you, eating it up.

593
00:30:09,791 --> 00:30:15,000
<i>On wings of song</i>

594
00:30:15,083 --> 00:30:20,750
<i>Fly to a place without pain or parting</i>

595
00:30:20,833 --> 00:30:26,458
<i>A garden of red blooms</i>

596
00:30:26,541 --> 00:30:30,750
<i>Dreaming under the quiet moonlight</i>

597
00:30:31,708 --> 00:30:37,541
<i>The lotus flowers</i>

598
00:30:37,625 --> 00:30:42,083
<i>Await their charming little sister</i>

599
00:30:42,166 --> 00:30:43,291
You like it?

600
00:30:44,416 --> 00:30:46,125
-I like.
-Yeah?

601
00:30:46,208 --> 00:30:47,041
Yes.

602
00:30:48,833 --> 00:30:49,791
Look.

603
00:30:51,666 --> 00:30:52,750
Do you like it?

604
00:31:02,416 --> 00:31:04,000
Make a heart.

605
00:31:04,083 --> 00:31:05,041
Heart.

606
00:31:06,208 --> 00:31:07,666
You like it, huh?

607
00:31:21,416 --> 00:31:22,583
Warden.

608
00:31:24,333 --> 00:31:25,291
8112.

609
00:31:25,375 --> 00:31:26,333
What are you doing?

610
00:31:26,416 --> 00:31:28,000
-Sorry.
-Know your place.

611
00:31:28,083 --> 00:31:29,083
It's okay. It's okay.

612
00:31:30,083 --> 00:31:30,916
You there.

613
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:32,000
You have a question?

614
00:31:33,500 --> 00:31:34,791
I have a question.

615
00:31:34,875 --> 00:31:37,666
Has this year's party program
been set?

616
00:31:38,791 --> 00:31:40,125
Is this year's decided?

617
00:31:40,208 --> 00:31:41,166
Not yet.

618
00:31:43,125 --> 00:31:44,416
What do you want to do?

619
00:31:44,500 --> 00:31:46,166
I'd like to perform with the choir.

620
00:31:46,791 --> 00:31:47,750
I want to sing.

621
00:31:48,291 --> 00:31:49,250
I just saw Yun-Shi

622
00:31:49,333 --> 00:31:50,958
listening to the choir.

623
00:31:51,458 --> 00:31:53,541
She looked happy, really into it.

624
00:31:54,250 --> 00:31:55,583
I want to learn to sing.

625
00:31:55,666 --> 00:31:56,541
Sir.

626
00:31:59,583 --> 00:32:01,083
That's not fair.

627
00:32:01,791 --> 00:32:03,041
We'd like to perform

628
00:32:03,125 --> 00:32:04,708
a dance too.

629
00:32:04,791 --> 00:32:06,166
Can you dance like that?

630
00:32:06,250 --> 00:32:08,166
I can. I can even wave, look.

631
00:32:10,666 --> 00:32:12,125
-Quiet.
-Okay.

632
00:32:12,666 --> 00:32:14,250
It's fine.

633
00:32:14,333 --> 00:32:17,708
Glad to see you all support the event.

634
00:32:17,791 --> 00:32:18,750
I'm happy too.

635
00:32:18,833 --> 00:32:21,541
But we do things fairly here.

636
00:32:21,625 --> 00:32:24,375
Discuss it between you.

637
00:32:24,458 --> 00:32:26,500
Pick one: dance

638
00:32:26,583 --> 00:32:27,583
or sing.

639
00:32:27,666 --> 00:32:29,291
Don't worry, Warden.

640
00:32:29,375 --> 00:32:32,000
In our dorm,
A-Pei sings great.

641
00:32:33,458 --> 00:32:34,458
And Grandma,

642
00:32:35,041 --> 00:32:37,166
she used to be a famous singer,

643
00:32:37,250 --> 00:32:38,916
and even led a choir.

644
00:32:39,000 --> 00:32:40,250
Nice. Good idea.

645
00:32:40,333 --> 00:32:42,625
Then, make a decision soon.

646
00:32:42,708 --> 00:32:44,666
-Okay.
-Thank you, sir.

647
00:32:44,750 --> 00:32:45,666
Goodbye, sir.

648
00:33:06,666 --> 00:33:07,666
Grandma.

649
00:33:07,750 --> 00:33:09,333
Sorry.

650
00:33:10,083 --> 00:33:12,583
I got ahead of myself.

651
00:33:12,666 --> 00:33:14,291
Sorry.

652
00:33:17,791 --> 00:33:19,333
Hui-Zhen,

653
00:33:19,416 --> 00:33:20,791
enough.

654
00:33:20,875 --> 00:33:22,000
You dragged me into it.

655
00:33:22,083 --> 00:33:24,625
Why bring Grandma into this?

656
00:33:24,708 --> 00:33:26,083
Yeah. You sing so badly.

657
00:33:26,166 --> 00:33:27,375
Why start a choir?

658
00:33:30,458 --> 00:33:31,500
Because…

659
00:33:32,666 --> 00:33:35,125
I've decided to send Yun-Shi out early.

660
00:33:39,125 --> 00:33:40,416
Isn't it two more years?

661
00:33:41,250 --> 00:33:43,375
Why the sudden change?

662
00:33:47,083 --> 00:33:48,125
Chief Fang.

663
00:33:48,958 --> 00:33:50,125
I think you're right.

664
00:33:51,708 --> 00:33:53,166
I want to help Yun-Shi

665
00:33:53,833 --> 00:33:55,250
find a new family.

666
00:33:56,916 --> 00:33:58,458
You mean,

667
00:33:58,541 --> 00:34:00,083
you'll send Yun-Shi away early?

668
00:34:05,500 --> 00:34:07,083
Because of her vision?

669
00:34:07,916 --> 00:34:09,875
I want to fix her eyes.

670
00:34:10,416 --> 00:34:13,375
Give her a better place to grow.

671
00:34:14,500 --> 00:34:17,375
That's what I should do as her mom.

672
00:34:17,458 --> 00:34:19,500
My only wish now

673
00:34:19,583 --> 00:34:23,541
is to form a choir.

674
00:34:24,666 --> 00:34:27,666
Give Yun-Shi a proper goodbye.

675
00:34:31,083 --> 00:34:31,958
Hey.

676
00:34:32,041 --> 00:34:32,875
All this time,

677
00:34:32,958 --> 00:34:34,625
just "Dear Michael"?

678
00:34:34,708 --> 00:34:36,958
Starting is hard.

679
00:34:37,041 --> 00:34:38,541
Your English is next level.

680
00:34:38,625 --> 00:34:39,750
I'll help you.

681
00:34:39,833 --> 00:34:41,125
Just write,

682
00:34:43,291 --> 00:34:44,625
"Miss you so much.

683
00:34:44,708 --> 00:34:48,041
My heart itches."

684
00:34:49,625 --> 00:34:50,458
Okay.

685
00:34:50,541 --> 00:34:52,083
I'll write, "going crazy."

686
00:34:52,166 --> 00:34:54,041
The itchy part stays in the heart.

687
00:34:54,125 --> 00:34:55,958
Chief Fang asked me to evaluate.

688
00:34:56,041 --> 00:34:58,500
Is Yun-Shi adjusting well?

689
00:34:58,583 --> 00:34:59,541
Pretty well.

690
00:35:00,916 --> 00:35:01,750
Here you go.

691
00:35:02,583 --> 00:35:04,916
What interests her most?

692
00:35:07,625 --> 00:35:09,750
She's quite into music.

693
00:35:09,833 --> 00:35:11,291
Music?

694
00:35:11,375 --> 00:35:12,541
That's great.

695
00:35:14,958 --> 00:35:17,208
Will she keep the eye patch on?

696
00:35:18,166 --> 00:35:19,750
She may try to rip it off, but…

697
00:35:19,833 --> 00:35:20,875
Out the way.

698
00:35:23,666 --> 00:35:24,625
Hey.

699
00:35:24,708 --> 00:35:26,083
What now?

700
00:35:26,708 --> 00:35:27,750
Something's up.

701
00:35:27,833 --> 00:35:28,916
-Go.
-What is it?

702
00:35:30,583 --> 00:35:32,125
Not enough people yet?

703
00:35:34,416 --> 00:35:35,541
None of your business.

704
00:35:36,666 --> 00:35:38,166
What do you want?

705
00:35:38,250 --> 00:35:39,875
-Get out.
-Relax.

706
00:35:39,958 --> 00:35:40,791
What?

707
00:35:40,875 --> 00:35:42,250
The warden wants us to talk.

708
00:35:42,333 --> 00:35:44,083
I'm talking.

709
00:35:44,166 --> 00:35:46,375
Last year was dance.
The year before too.

710
00:35:46,458 --> 00:35:47,958
You damn idiot.

711
00:35:48,041 --> 00:35:49,208
Telling the warden?

712
00:35:49,291 --> 00:35:50,875
Know how long I trained?

713
00:35:50,958 --> 00:35:53,458
Yeah. Sister Wang trained for half a year.

714
00:35:53,541 --> 00:35:55,958
To score points at the party.
Level up early.

715
00:35:56,041 --> 00:35:57,625
Want points?
Join the choir.

716
00:35:57,708 --> 00:35:58,958
Fuck me.

717
00:35:59,500 --> 00:36:01,375
Singing isn't the same as dancing.

718
00:36:03,500 --> 00:36:05,375
Got a brat,
think you're better than us?

719
00:36:05,458 --> 00:36:06,583
Who's the brat?

720
00:36:07,166 --> 00:36:09,541
-Who?
-Separate, all of you.

721
00:36:09,625 --> 00:36:10,708
It's fine.

722
00:36:10,791 --> 00:36:12,250
-Watch it.
-Watch it.

723
00:36:12,750 --> 00:36:13,625
Hey.

724
00:36:14,333 --> 00:36:15,708
Even if it's dance,

725
00:36:15,791 --> 00:36:16,958
I'll sign up for dance.

726
00:36:17,625 --> 00:36:18,583
But the points

727
00:36:18,666 --> 00:36:19,875
will be mine.

728
00:36:20,500 --> 00:36:21,416
So mean.

729
00:36:23,958 --> 00:36:25,541
Back when I ruled the disco,

730
00:36:25,625 --> 00:36:27,458
you weren't even born.

731
00:36:27,958 --> 00:36:29,333
Then show us.

732
00:36:29,416 --> 00:36:31,000
-Bring it on!
-Not afraid of you!

733
00:36:31,083 --> 00:36:31,916
Can you do it?

734
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:33,125
Come on.

735
00:36:37,708 --> 00:36:38,750
Sir, let us work out.

736
00:36:39,458 --> 00:36:40,791
Exercise.

737
00:36:42,916 --> 00:36:44,875
Just do it. What's the hold up?

738
00:36:57,250 --> 00:36:58,250
Show her.

739
00:37:21,166 --> 00:37:22,375
See that?

740
00:37:23,083 --> 00:37:24,416
Seems pretty good.

741
00:37:49,791 --> 00:37:51,375
We won.

742
00:37:55,291 --> 00:37:56,458
Got long legs, so what?

743
00:37:56,541 --> 00:37:57,458
What?

744
00:37:57,541 --> 00:37:59,041
What are you doing?

745
00:37:59,125 --> 00:38:00,583
You a sore loser.

746
00:38:02,000 --> 00:38:03,125
What the hell?

747
00:38:03,208 --> 00:38:04,708
Exercise time is over.

748
00:38:05,375 --> 00:38:06,416
Fall in.

749
00:38:07,500 --> 00:38:08,458
Still staring?

750
00:38:10,416 --> 00:38:11,791
Line up.

751
00:38:13,958 --> 00:38:15,000
Take your seats.

752
00:38:23,458 --> 00:38:24,583
What's that?

753
00:38:24,666 --> 00:38:25,500
You didn't see?

754
00:38:25,583 --> 00:38:27,416
Middle-school diploma.

755
00:38:27,500 --> 00:38:29,708
-My son graduated?
-Nice.

756
00:38:29,791 --> 00:38:31,791
-Two weeks ago.
-All right.

757
00:38:32,416 --> 00:38:35,541
When you pulled that out,
you scared me here.

758
00:38:35,625 --> 00:38:38,875
-Thought it was a marriage cert.
-I'm innocent, Your Honor.

759
00:38:38,958 --> 00:38:40,458
Are you doing honest work?

760
00:38:40,541 --> 00:38:42,208
-No more scams.
-No.

761
00:38:42,291 --> 00:38:44,041
If you return, who watches the kid?

762
00:38:44,125 --> 00:38:45,708
Keep it down.
I'm done with that.

763
00:38:45,791 --> 00:38:48,000
Good. Hey.

764
00:38:48,083 --> 00:38:50,875
Bring more food next visit.

765
00:38:50,958 --> 00:38:53,333
Yun-Shi wants chicken drumsticks.

766
00:38:53,416 --> 00:38:55,916
They're always starving.

767
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:57,541
Buy two kg, or more.

768
00:39:00,333 --> 00:39:02,916
It's been about ten years?

769
00:39:04,666 --> 00:39:07,000
All these years, I came to see you,

770
00:39:07,083 --> 00:39:08,750
and you refused my visits.

771
00:39:09,750 --> 00:39:12,375
Why agree to see me now?

772
00:39:14,625 --> 00:39:16,833
Whatever your reason,
it doesn't matter.

773
00:39:16,958 --> 00:39:20,833
I'll still come every year
around this time.

774
00:39:22,041 --> 00:39:23,833
-Because today is--
-The day he died.

775
00:39:26,416 --> 00:39:28,666
The anniversary
of your brother Zhi-Wei's death.

776
00:39:31,458 --> 00:39:32,708
I know.

777
00:39:38,250 --> 00:39:40,416
<i>Also the day you killed Dad</i>

778
00:39:41,500 --> 00:39:43,541
<i>and wrecked my life.</i>

779
00:40:25,291 --> 00:40:26,291
Once more.

780
00:40:28,750 --> 00:40:30,000
Push.

781
00:41:11,125 --> 00:41:13,583
Mom.

782
00:41:14,541 --> 00:41:16,958
<i>You tried to die, but you failed.</i>

783
00:41:17,041 --> 00:41:18,833
<i>And just like that, you were gone.</i>

784
00:41:19,958 --> 00:41:20,916
<i>What about me?</i>

785
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:22,291
<i>When I was a kid,</i>

786
00:41:22,375 --> 00:41:24,291
<i>the media hounded me all day,</i>

787
00:41:24,375 --> 00:41:26,250
reporters chasing me with questions.

788
00:41:26,333 --> 00:41:28,958
<i>"Why did your celebrity mom murder?"</i>

789
00:41:29,625 --> 00:41:31,625
<i>I lived like a street rat.</i>

790
00:41:32,750 --> 00:41:34,416
<i>Did you know that?</i>

791
00:41:39,625 --> 00:41:42,791
<i>Till we meet again</i>

792
00:41:42,875 --> 00:41:45,500
<i>Take my hand</i>

793
00:41:45,583 --> 00:41:49,541
<i>Watch the warm sunset</i>

794
00:41:49,666 --> 00:41:52,333
<i>As it crosses the hills</i>

795
00:41:52,416 --> 00:41:55,541
{\an8}<i>The world is wide</i>

796
00:41:55,625 --> 00:41:58,916
{\an8}<i>I want to walk with you</i>

797
00:41:59,000 --> 00:42:01,708
<i>But time</i>

798
00:42:01,791 --> 00:42:04,541
<i>Always arrives first</i>

799
00:42:04,625 --> 00:42:06,500
<i>To the end</i>

800
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:09,791
Mom.

801
00:42:13,750 --> 00:42:15,375
Mom.

802
00:42:23,666 --> 00:42:25,708
Mom.

803
00:42:25,791 --> 00:42:28,375
Yang Yu-Ying.
Take a look yourself.

804
00:42:28,458 --> 00:42:30,583
You sing and play the piano every day.

805
00:42:30,666 --> 00:42:32,208
Look how you raised the kid.

806
00:42:32,291 --> 00:42:33,916
What kind of mother are you?

807
00:42:34,000 --> 00:42:36,833
PHENYLKETONURIA
MAY CAUSE INTELLECTUAL DISABILITY

808
00:42:38,291 --> 00:42:39,375
What are you doing?

809
00:42:39,458 --> 00:42:40,875
-What the hell?
-Who are you?

810
00:42:40,958 --> 00:42:42,375
Damn it.

811
00:42:43,416 --> 00:42:45,750
You think you're still that big star
on stage?

812
00:42:45,833 --> 00:42:46,791
Keep dreaming.

813
00:42:47,541 --> 00:42:48,666
I'm a doctor,

814
00:42:48,750 --> 00:42:50,333
and you let me lose face.

815
00:42:50,416 --> 00:42:51,791
What the hell?

816
00:42:52,416 --> 00:42:54,166
Keep your kid under control.

817
00:42:54,250 --> 00:42:55,958
Can't even have a normal kid.

818
00:42:56,583 --> 00:42:58,583
You shouldn't have been born.

819
00:42:59,166 --> 00:43:02,125
Why don't you just die?

820
00:43:24,208 --> 00:43:27,125
<i>Till we meet again</i>

821
00:43:27,208 --> 00:43:30,500
<i>Kiss my forehead</i>

822
00:43:30,583 --> 00:43:33,916
<i>The clear sky will</i>

823
00:43:34,000 --> 00:43:36,541
<i>Embrace you and me</i>

824
00:43:36,625 --> 00:43:38,333
<i>If not for you,</i>

825
00:43:38,416 --> 00:43:40,416
<i>I wouldn't have been this strong.</i>

826
00:43:40,500 --> 00:43:42,416
<i>Every year on this day,</i>

827
00:43:42,500 --> 00:43:43,916
<i>I'll come to torment you,</i>

828
00:43:44,000 --> 00:43:46,708
<i>to remind you,</i>
<i>so you always remember,</i>

829
00:43:46,791 --> 00:43:49,625
<i>what a cruel, awful mother you are.</i>

830
00:44:09,875 --> 00:44:10,833
Grandma.

831
00:44:12,250 --> 00:44:14,208
You still like music, right?

832
00:44:14,291 --> 00:44:15,583
Please help me, okay?

833
00:44:15,666 --> 00:44:17,458
The audition's tomorrow. I need you.

834
00:44:17,541 --> 00:44:18,583
No.

835
00:44:18,666 --> 00:44:20,958
I said no.

836
00:44:22,000 --> 00:44:23,083
That's…

837
00:44:24,000 --> 00:44:25,083
enough.

838
00:44:33,625 --> 00:44:35,416
-Can you do this?
-Hold still.

839
00:44:35,500 --> 00:44:36,833
You take so long.

840
00:44:36,916 --> 00:44:38,458
-Damn it.
-Seriously.

841
00:44:38,541 --> 00:44:40,125
