-Hey, wait for me.

1379
01:12:55,666 --> 01:12:57,666
Tseng Zi-Ching, wait up.

1380
01:12:57,750 --> 01:13:00,333
Fen-Fen, hurry. You're so slow.

1381
01:13:02,416 --> 01:13:04,125
Chicken drumstick bento.

1382
01:13:05,083 --> 01:13:06,416
I'm coming.

1383
01:13:07,833 --> 01:13:08,666
Wait for me.

1384
01:13:12,375 --> 01:13:13,208
Smells so good.

1385
01:13:13,291 --> 01:13:15,166
Hurry up.

1386
01:13:15,250 --> 01:13:16,250
Hurry.

1387
01:13:18,916 --> 01:13:20,750
Two chicken drumstick bento, please.

1388
01:13:24,625 --> 01:13:26,666
Wow, so many toppings.

1389
01:13:26,750 --> 01:13:27,833
Thank you.

1390
01:13:28,750 --> 01:13:31,375
-Hey, you got two mains. Trade with me.
-No.

1391
01:13:31,458 --> 01:13:32,916
-Come on, don't be stingy.
-No.

1392
01:13:33,000 --> 01:13:34,750
That's for running so slow.

1393
01:13:42,458 --> 01:13:43,583
Mom.

1394
01:13:47,208 --> 01:13:48,041
Auntie.

1395
01:14:00,583 --> 01:14:07,375
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

1396
01:14:08,125 --> 01:14:10,041
Make a wish.

1397
01:14:12,625 --> 01:14:14,000
Happy birthday.

1398
01:14:14,083 --> 01:14:15,375
Come on.

1399
01:14:15,458 --> 01:14:17,166
Let's cut the cake.

1400
01:14:17,250 --> 01:14:18,333
By the way.

1401
01:14:18,750 --> 01:14:20,375
Next week's showcase.

1402
01:14:20,458 --> 01:14:21,458
Will you two come?

1403
01:14:21,541 --> 01:14:22,875
Of course.

1404
01:14:22,958 --> 01:14:24,458
Didn't we promise you?

1405
01:14:26,250 --> 01:14:28,125
Can I invite one more person?

1406
01:14:28,208 --> 01:14:29,375
Who?

1407
01:14:31,416 --> 01:14:32,750
My birth mom.

1408
01:14:35,000 --> 01:14:36,333
Zi-Ching.

1409
01:14:36,416 --> 01:14:38,916
About that, we think that if--

1410
01:14:39,000 --> 01:14:40,791
I'll try to contact her.

1411
01:14:40,875 --> 01:14:41,875
Really?

1412
01:14:43,916 --> 01:14:45,791
But…

1413
01:14:45,875 --> 01:14:48,291
It's been many years.
She hasn't showed up once.

1414
01:14:48,375 --> 01:14:50,500
{\an8}I can't promise she'll come.

1415
01:15:21,041 --> 01:15:23,000
I went to see Yun-Shi for you.

1416
01:15:23,083 --> 01:15:24,208
She's doing well now.

1417
01:15:24,291 --> 01:15:25,750
Her eye treatment continues.

1418
01:15:26,666 --> 01:15:27,916
Don't worry.

1419
01:15:28,000 --> 01:15:29,708
Thank you.

1420
01:15:30,291 --> 01:15:31,375
It's nothing.

1421
01:15:31,458 --> 01:15:33,375
I wanted to know how she was, too.

1422
01:15:35,291 --> 01:15:36,875
By the way, supervisor.

1423
01:15:37,625 --> 01:15:39,000
I've been wanting to ask.

1424
01:15:39,708 --> 01:15:41,916
Why do you look out for Yun-Shi and me?

1425
01:15:47,416 --> 01:15:50,083
You've got the courage I never had.

1426
01:15:54,291 --> 01:15:56,166
Back then, I wasn't brave enough.

1427
01:15:57,000 --> 01:15:58,666
I didn't have my child.

1428
01:16:04,500 --> 01:16:06,375
But I had her.

1429
01:16:07,041 --> 01:16:09,375
I didn't give her a healthy body.

1430
01:16:09,458 --> 01:16:11,541
I couldn't care for her.

1431
01:16:12,375 --> 01:16:14,083
Is that really right?

1432
01:16:14,166 --> 01:16:16,750
At least you gave her a future.

1433
01:16:17,875 --> 01:16:20,541
By the way,
Yun-Shi's been out for over two years.

1434
01:16:20,625 --> 01:16:23,125
No one's adopted her yet.

1435
01:16:23,208 --> 01:16:25,083
Is it because

1436
01:16:25,166 --> 01:16:26,666
her mother is a murderer?

1437
01:16:27,791 --> 01:16:29,625
Finding a new family

1438
01:16:29,708 --> 01:16:31,666
takes fate.

1439
01:16:33,416 --> 01:16:34,833
Don't worry.

1440
01:16:35,708 --> 01:16:36,541
Hui-Zhen.

1441
01:16:36,625 --> 01:16:38,750
Stop talking. Come play.

1442
01:16:41,875 --> 01:16:42,958
Assemble.

1443
01:16:50,833 --> 01:16:52,458
I have an announcement.

1444
01:16:53,375 --> 01:16:54,333
The warden

1445
01:16:54,416 --> 01:16:56,583
has recommended Sunshine Women's Choir

1446
01:16:56,666 --> 01:16:58,375
to perform at the Hope Concert.

1447
01:17:00,291 --> 01:17:02,416
Did I sing too well?

1448
01:17:03,375 --> 01:17:04,833
You done? Zip it.

1449
01:17:05,583 --> 01:17:08,541
In two months, during Mother's Day week,

1450
01:17:08,625 --> 01:17:11,958
you'll represent the women's prison
at a concert.

1451
01:17:12,541 --> 01:17:14,125
Does this mean we leave?

1452
01:17:14,208 --> 01:17:15,208
Duh.

1453
01:17:16,041 --> 01:17:18,041
Michael, I'm coming.

1454
01:17:19,208 --> 01:17:20,125
Quiet.

1455
01:17:21,916 --> 01:17:23,000
8112.

1456
01:17:23,083 --> 01:17:24,208
Yes.

1457
01:17:25,083 --> 01:17:26,583
You must participate.

1458
01:17:27,375 --> 01:17:28,208
I…

1459
01:17:30,583 --> 01:17:31,666
Chief Fang.

1460
01:17:32,666 --> 01:17:33,666
I don't want to.

1461
01:17:33,750 --> 01:17:35,625
Who are you to say no?

1462
01:17:36,291 --> 01:17:37,458
Officers.

1463
01:17:37,541 --> 01:17:38,750
Take them back.

1464
01:17:38,833 --> 01:17:40,416
-Dismissed.
-Yes.

1465
01:17:43,041 --> 01:17:44,500
8024.

1466
01:17:44,583 --> 01:17:45,708
Take your meds.

1467
01:17:49,125 --> 01:17:50,166
Thanks.

1468
01:17:58,291 --> 01:17:59,500
Attention, everyone.

1469
01:18:03,541 --> 01:18:04,500
8918.

1470
01:18:05,250 --> 01:18:06,875
-Visitation.
-Me?

1471
01:18:06,958 --> 01:18:08,791
You doubt me?
Are you coming or not?

1472
01:18:19,500 --> 01:18:20,666
You-Xin.

1473
01:18:22,750 --> 01:18:24,333
You-Xin.

1474
01:18:25,791 --> 01:18:26,708
You…

1475
01:18:26,791 --> 01:18:28,000
Who are you?

1476
01:18:28,083 --> 01:18:29,291
I…

1477
01:18:30,625 --> 01:18:32,208
I'm your mother.

1478
01:18:33,333 --> 01:18:34,458
I'm sorry.

1479
01:18:35,375 --> 01:18:37,041
I only recently learned

1480
01:18:37,125 --> 01:18:39,125
what happened to you.

1481
01:18:40,250 --> 01:18:41,708
I miss you so much.

1482
01:18:42,833 --> 01:18:44,500
I wanted to see you.

1483
01:18:51,333 --> 01:18:52,625
I want to ask you…

1484
01:18:54,000 --> 01:18:55,458
Did you know

1485
01:18:55,541 --> 01:18:57,208
Grandma left you

1486
01:18:59,875 --> 01:19:02,000
the house in her will?

1487
01:19:02,083 --> 01:19:03,458
Do you know this?

1488
01:19:06,708 --> 01:19:07,958
So what if I know?

1489
01:19:08,041 --> 01:19:09,250
Or don't?

1490
01:19:09,833 --> 01:19:11,875
I think

1491
01:19:13,083 --> 01:19:14,250
since

1492
01:19:14,333 --> 01:19:15,208
you are, well,

1493
01:19:15,291 --> 01:19:17,666
you're inside right now.

1494
01:19:18,458 --> 01:19:19,416
About the house,

1495
01:19:19,500 --> 01:19:21,958
could you
sign it over to me?

1496
01:19:23,083 --> 01:19:23,916
You…

1497
01:19:24,458 --> 01:19:25,291
You-Xin.

1498
01:19:26,041 --> 01:19:27,291
Don't get me wrong.

1499
01:19:27,375 --> 01:19:29,291
If we rent the place out,

1500
01:19:29,375 --> 01:19:31,041
we can make money.

1501
01:19:31,125 --> 01:19:34,000
I'll give the house back when you get out.

1502
01:19:34,083 --> 01:19:35,125
Okay?

1503
01:19:35,208 --> 01:19:36,625
Stop lying.

1504
01:19:36,708 --> 01:19:38,000
You ditched me as a kid.

1505
01:19:38,083 --> 01:19:39,291
Never checked on me.

1506
01:19:39,833 --> 01:19:42,208
You were nowhere when Grandma
and Dad died.

1507
01:19:42,291 --> 01:19:44,666
How dare you show up asking for the house?

1508
01:19:45,208 --> 01:19:46,875
You only care about money, not me.

1509
01:19:46,958 --> 01:19:48,541
8918, attention.

1510
01:19:48,625 --> 01:19:49,958
Quiet, or the visit ends.

1511
01:19:50,041 --> 01:19:51,000
You-Xin.

1512
01:19:51,083 --> 01:19:54,375
My life has been so hard. You…

1513
01:19:54,458 --> 01:19:57,291
Think about when I had you.

1514
01:19:57,375 --> 01:19:59,958
I still had to care
for your useless father.

1515
01:20:00,041 --> 01:20:02,375
Your grandma was selfish too.

1516
01:20:02,458 --> 01:20:03,708
You wouldn't have suffered

1517
01:20:03,791 --> 01:20:05,791
if she'd sold it earlier.

1518
01:20:06,416 --> 01:20:08,625
You're obsessed with money.

1519
01:20:08,708 --> 01:20:11,791
If it sold, where would we have lived?
Sleep on the street?

1520
01:20:11,875 --> 01:20:14,250
How much is that place even worth?

1521
01:20:14,333 --> 01:20:16,083
It couldn't pay for Dad's treatment.

1522
01:20:16,166 --> 01:20:18,166
No, no. You don't know.

1523
01:20:18,250 --> 01:20:21,000
A developer is interested in the land.

1524
01:20:21,083 --> 01:20:23,791
For luxury condos. Worth a lot.

1525
01:20:24,583 --> 01:20:27,041
When you get out,

1526
01:20:27,125 --> 01:20:28,916
we'll split it fifty-fifty.

1527
01:20:29,000 --> 01:20:30,125
Fifty-fifty okay?

1528
01:20:48,250 --> 01:20:49,166
What's wrong?

1529
01:20:51,541 --> 01:20:52,750
What happened?

1530
01:20:53,625 --> 01:20:54,583
Come.

1531
01:20:55,291 --> 01:20:56,625
Tell Grandma.

1532
01:21:01,500 --> 01:21:03,208
Why?

1533
01:21:04,333 --> 01:21:07,750
Why do I have a mom like this?

1534
01:21:09,333 --> 01:21:11,541
I really hate her.

1535
01:21:14,250 --> 01:21:15,166
Why?

1536
01:21:16,208 --> 01:21:17,583
Don't cry.

1537
01:21:19,708 --> 01:21:20,833
Don't cry.

1538
01:21:22,291 --> 01:21:24,541
She probably doesn't know

1539
01:21:25,541 --> 01:21:28,375
how to be a mother yet.

1540
01:21:45,333 --> 01:21:47,625
Is Grandma okay?
Why the shot?

1541
01:21:49,375 --> 01:21:51,000
She's just seeing the doctor.

1542
01:21:51,083 --> 01:21:52,166
Don't worry.

1543
01:21:53,750 --> 01:21:54,750
Let's go.

1544
01:21:56,125 --> 01:21:58,625
I called you here to tell you.

1545
01:21:59,500 --> 01:22:00,791
Yun-Shi found a family.

1546
01:22:04,208 --> 01:22:05,166
She did?

1547
01:22:07,458 --> 01:22:08,458
What…

1548
01:22:08,916 --> 01:22:10,375
What kind of people are they?

1549
01:22:10,458 --> 01:22:11,833
Any other kids?

1550
01:22:11,958 --> 01:22:13,166
What do they do?

1551
01:22:13,250 --> 01:22:14,666
Here, this is her file.

1552
01:22:16,000 --> 01:22:18,125
{\an8}Social Services matched many families

1553
01:22:18,208 --> 01:22:19,916
{\an8}and assessed her as the best fit.

1554
01:22:27,208 --> 01:22:31,166
{\an8}NO CRIMINAL RECORD

1555
01:22:37,916 --> 01:22:39,166
Next,

1556
01:22:39,250 --> 01:22:41,083
the court will summon you.

1557
01:22:41,166 --> 01:22:44,166
You can meet her in person.

1558
01:22:52,250 --> 01:22:53,458
Great.

1559
01:23:12,416 --> 01:23:13,875
I need the restroom.

1560
01:23:52,833 --> 01:23:54,083
Grandma.

1561
01:23:57,000 --> 01:23:58,000
Are you okay?

1562
01:24:00,208 --> 01:24:03,791
Just old age.
Don't worry.

1563
01:24:04,875 --> 01:24:05,708
Grandma.

1564
01:24:06,208 --> 01:24:08,875
I passed the infirmary
and saw you on an IV.

1565
01:24:08,958 --> 01:24:10,583
You're on more meds too.

1566
01:24:10,666 --> 01:24:11,708
Are you sick?

1567
01:24:11,791 --> 01:24:12,875
It's nothing.

1568
01:24:13,666 --> 01:24:15,250
Don't worry.

1569
01:24:15,333 --> 01:24:16,958
I'm really worried.

1570
01:24:18,083 --> 01:24:19,166
Grandma.

1571
01:24:19,250 --> 01:24:20,916
This is serious.

1572
01:24:21,000 --> 01:24:22,708
I'll ask the supervisor

1573
01:24:22,791 --> 01:24:24,666
so you can see a doctor outside.

1574
01:24:32,333 --> 01:24:33,375
Okay?

1575
01:24:34,791 --> 01:24:35,833
Hui-Zhen.

1576
01:24:38,666 --> 01:24:39,791
I have liver cancer.

1577
01:24:40,666 --> 01:24:41,750
It's terminal.

1578
01:24:52,916 --> 01:24:55,375
The tests show stage two liver cancer.

1579
01:24:55,458 --> 01:24:56,583
Well…

1580
01:24:57,250 --> 01:24:59,750
I suggest a hospital outside
for more detailed tests.

1581
01:24:59,833 --> 01:25:02,958
Then we'll know how to treat it.

1582
01:25:04,125 --> 01:25:06,041
For liver cancer, a family donor

1583
01:25:06,125 --> 01:25:07,375
is also an option.

1584
01:25:09,250 --> 01:25:11,333
We can contact your family about that.

1585
01:25:12,208 --> 01:25:13,250
It's up to you.

1586
01:25:15,166 --> 01:25:16,083
8024.

1587
01:25:20,666 --> 01:25:21,500
Yes.

1588
01:25:24,458 --> 01:25:26,041
I can help contact your daughter.

1589
01:25:32,416 --> 01:25:33,583
Chief Fang.

1590
01:25:34,583 --> 01:25:36,708
Thanks. Thank you.

1591
01:25:37,750 --> 01:25:38,666
I don't want to

1592
01:25:39,375 --> 01:25:42,083
be a burden to my family.

1593
01:25:42,958 --> 01:25:44,166
Also,

1594
01:25:45,041 --> 01:25:47,416
please don't tell others

1595
01:25:48,875 --> 01:25:50,250
that I'm sick.

1596
01:25:52,583 --> 01:25:53,500
Please.

1597
01:25:57,083 --> 01:25:57,916
Okay.

1598
01:26:02,000 --> 01:26:05,291
<i>I even thought about ending my life.</i>

1599
01:26:06,500 --> 01:26:07,416
<i>But…</i>

1600
01:26:08,958 --> 01:26:09,916
because of you…

1601
01:26:11,333 --> 01:26:13,250
seeing you form this choir

1602
01:26:13,333 --> 01:26:16,000
<i>for your daughter</i>

1603
01:26:16,083 --> 01:26:18,291
<i>and asking me to conduct…</i>

1604
01:26:19,166 --> 01:26:20,625
<i>Because of you,</i>

1605
01:26:21,416 --> 01:26:23,500
<i>I found music again.</i>

1606
01:26:24,833 --> 01:26:26,208
I want to thank you.

1607
01:26:27,500 --> 01:26:29,458
I can still make

1608
01:26:30,625 --> 01:26:33,666
my final moments meaningful.

1609
01:26:35,083 --> 01:26:36,750
This was the time

1610
01:26:37,625 --> 01:26:40,250
I felt most human.

1611
01:26:42,958 --> 01:26:45,458
It also
reminded me

1612
01:26:47,666 --> 01:26:49,125
of who I used to be…

1613
01:26:52,333 --> 01:26:53,625
the singer

1614
01:26:56,041 --> 01:26:57,625
Julian.

1615
01:27:11,666 --> 01:27:13,000
I know.

1616
01:27:13,083 --> 01:27:15,791
I won't leave this place alive.

1617
01:27:15,875 --> 01:27:16,708
Don't say that.

1618
01:27:16,791 --> 01:27:18,583
Really, I won't.

1619
01:27:19,250 --> 01:27:20,375
So…

1620
01:27:21,708 --> 01:27:24,333
I want to go out with the choir

1621
01:27:25,208 --> 01:27:27,375
and see the world

1622
01:27:28,250 --> 01:27:29,791
one last time.

1623
01:27:31,250 --> 01:27:33,375
Okay.

1624
01:27:44,958 --> 01:27:48,708
<i>The wind of growing up</i>

1625
01:27:48,791 --> 01:27:52,791
<i>Gently blows</i>

1626
01:27:52,875 --> 01:27:59,375
<i>Carrying the past forward</i>

1627
01:28:00,500 --> 01:28:03,625
<i>Evening dew, morning bloom</i>

1628
01:28:04,500 --> 01:28:07,583
<i>Lightly kissing the world</i>

1629
01:28:07,666 --> 01:28:09,666
<i>Smiling at the past</i>

1630
01:28:09,750 --> 01:28:11,875
Long Legs, this one's you.

1631
01:28:13,208 --> 01:28:16,083
Your families can get tickets.
Remember to tell them.

1632
01:28:16,166 --> 01:28:22,666
<i>Tears fall from the sky</i>

1633
01:28:23,541 --> 01:28:30,208
<i>Longing blooms on the ground</i>

1634
01:28:30,916 --> 01:28:37,791
<i>People part in a hurry</i>

1635
01:28:38,250 --> 01:28:45,041
<i>Who knows when we'll meet again</i>

1636
01:28:45,583 --> 01:28:47,083
Did you get your tickets?

1637
01:28:47,166 --> 01:28:49,666
Relax. No problem.

1638
01:28:50,708 --> 01:28:53,916
Been a while since you kissed me.

1639
01:28:54,000 --> 01:28:55,458
HU MEI-HUA

1640
01:29:08,333 --> 01:29:11,291
Are you the birth mother
Ms. Li Hui-Zhen?

1641
01:29:11,375 --> 01:29:12,833
Is that Yun-Shi?

1642
01:29:12,916 --> 01:29:14,208
Yes.

1643
01:29:15,083 --> 01:29:15,916
Where is she?

1644
01:29:16,625 --> 01:29:18,583
She's in the temporary nursery.

1645
01:29:19,458 --> 01:29:21,083
So…

1646
01:29:21,166 --> 01:29:22,875
I can't see her?

1647
01:29:22,958 --> 01:29:23,791
No.

1648
01:29:24,541 --> 01:29:26,041
Ms. Li Hui-Zhen.

1649
01:29:26,125 --> 01:29:28,416
Do you agree to place your child,
Li Yun-Shi,

1650
01:29:28,500 --> 01:29:30,875
in the care of Ms. Tseng Ya-Han?

1651
01:29:36,416 --> 01:29:38,916
Ms. Tseng.

1652
01:29:39,000 --> 01:29:40,333
Please.

1653
01:29:40,416 --> 01:29:42,625
You must fix Yun-Shi's eye,

1654
01:29:42,708 --> 01:29:43,875
okay?

1655
01:29:43,958 --> 01:29:45,541
I will.

1656
01:29:46,416 --> 01:29:47,375
Ms. Li Hui-Zhen.

1657
01:29:47,458 --> 01:29:48,750
Thank you.

1658
01:29:48,833 --> 01:29:51,333
If you agree,

1659
01:29:51,416 --> 01:29:54,250
you will no longer have custody
of your child.

1660
01:29:54,333 --> 01:29:55,208
Legally,

1661
01:29:55,291 --> 01:29:57,291
you will no longer be her mother.

1662
01:29:58,166 --> 01:30:01,625
<i>Tears fall from the sky</i>

1663
01:30:01,708 --> 01:30:03,291
No trouble outside.

1664
01:30:03,375 --> 01:30:05,166
I won't go easy on anyone.

1665
01:30:05,250 --> 01:30:12,250
<i>Longing blooms on the ground</i>

1666
01:30:12,916 --> 01:30:19,916
<i>People part in a hurry</i>

1667
01:30:20,416 --> 01:30:26,166
<i>Who knows when we'll meet again</i>

1668
01:30:27,875 --> 01:30:34,000
<i>Lovers, don't say goodbye</i>

1669
01:30:35,875 --> 01:30:38,125
<i>Who knows when we'll meet again</i>

1670
01:30:38,208 --> 01:30:39,541
Get off in order.

1671
01:30:39,625 --> 01:30:40,458
No pushing.

1672
01:30:42,666 --> 01:30:45,416
Gosh, we're famous.

1673
01:30:45,500 --> 01:30:47,291
-Hello, this way.
-Move quickly.

1674
01:30:48,791 --> 01:30:49,625
Head inside.

1675
01:30:49,708 --> 01:30:51,250
Move.

1676
01:30:51,333 --> 01:30:53,000
Everyone, attention.

1677
01:30:53,083 --> 01:30:56,625
Heads down, no looking around,
no talking.

1678
01:30:56,750 --> 01:30:58,000
Go.

1679
01:30:58,083 --> 01:30:59,291
Line up and move forward.

1680
01:31:01,375 --> 01:31:02,625
HOPE CONCERT

1681
01:31:03,583 --> 01:31:05,208
Hey, look.

1682
01:31:07,416 --> 01:31:08,250
Dad.

1683
01:31:08,333 --> 01:31:09,166
Our seats.

1684
01:31:09,250 --> 01:31:10,083
Over here.

1685
01:31:10,166 --> 01:31:11,333
Okay, you sit in first.

1686
01:31:11,416 --> 01:31:12,916
Come on. Wait.

1687
01:31:13,000 --> 01:31:14,166
You sit here.

1688
01:31:14,250 --> 01:31:15,291
You sit here.

1689
01:31:18,166 --> 01:31:19,000
Like this.

1690
01:31:19,083 --> 01:31:20,875
Talk faster.

1691
01:31:22,916 --> 01:31:24,083
Wearing pigtails today.

1692
01:31:24,958 --> 01:31:26,208
Can I use the restroom?

1693
01:31:26,291 --> 01:31:28,208
-I need to go too.
-Me too.

1694
01:31:28,291 --> 01:31:29,833
Okay, hold on.

1695
01:31:29,916 --> 01:31:31,833
I'll say this one last time.

1696
01:31:31,916 --> 01:31:33,458
If anyone slips up,

1697
01:31:33,541 --> 01:31:34,833
no more show.

1698
01:31:35,541 --> 01:31:37,666
We move together. Everyone goes at once.

1699
01:31:37,750 --> 01:31:40,041
After we return, no more restroom trips.

1700
01:31:40,125 --> 01:31:42,208
-Understood?
-Understood.

1701
01:31:42,291 --> 01:31:43,958
Line up for the restroom.

1702
01:31:44,041 --> 01:31:45,291
Get to the front.

1703
01:31:45,375 --> 01:31:47,166
Okay, slowly.

1704
01:31:52,250 --> 01:31:54,541
Move to the side.
To the side.

1705
01:31:54,625 --> 01:31:56,083
Why are there inmates here?

1706
01:31:56,708 --> 01:31:58,708
What are they doing at a concert?

1707
01:32:02,666 --> 01:32:03,791
Just keep to the side.

1708
01:32:04,416 --> 01:32:06,000
No need to face the wall.

1709
01:32:06,083 --> 01:32:07,333
You need to be clear.

1710
01:32:07,416 --> 01:32:08,791
It's just a force of habit.

1711
01:32:09,750 --> 01:32:12,458
-Reflex.
-Too well-trained.

1712
01:32:12,541 --> 01:32:13,541
Faster.

1713
01:32:18,083 --> 01:32:20,166
Restroom.

1714
01:32:20,250 --> 01:32:21,958
I can't hold it.

1715
01:32:22,041 --> 01:32:23,541
Wait a sec.

1716
01:32:25,041 --> 01:32:26,500
So in a hurry.

1717
01:32:26,583 --> 01:32:28,250
-For Grandma.
-Where's Sister Wang?

1718
01:32:29,125 --> 01:32:29,958
Director-General.

1719
01:32:31,250 --> 01:32:33,291
Greetings.

1720
01:32:34,500 --> 01:32:36,583
-Hello, Director-General.
-Hello, sir.

1721
01:32:36,666 --> 01:32:39,583
Welcome, distinguished guests,
to the Hope Charity Concert

1722
01:32:39,666 --> 01:32:44,458
hosted by the Star Gen Foundation
and the Agency of Corrections.

1723
01:32:46,750 --> 01:32:49,083
I'm sure you're all excited.

1724
01:32:50,000 --> 01:32:52,958
Please take your seats promptly.

1725
01:32:53,041 --> 01:32:55,291
Thank you for your cooperation.

1726
01:32:59,666 --> 01:33:00,875
-All right.
-It's fine.

1727
01:33:00,958 --> 01:33:03,083
You look good. You fine.

1728
01:33:03,791 --> 01:33:04,666
Nobody move.

1729
01:33:06,708 --> 01:33:08,541
Is something wrong?

1730
01:33:09,416 --> 01:33:10,666
There's been a theft.

1731
01:33:11,416 --> 01:33:12,750
Everyone, on your feet.

1732
01:33:12,833 --> 01:33:14,125
Wait, what evidence?

1733
01:33:14,208 --> 01:33:16,125
Search.

1734
01:33:16,791 --> 01:33:18,791
-Search what?
-Shut up.

1735
01:33:19,666 --> 01:33:20,916
Everyone,

1736
01:33:21,000 --> 01:33:22,541
you were in the ladies' room.

1737
01:33:22,625 --> 01:33:24,500
We have reason to suspect you of theft.

1738
01:33:24,583 --> 01:33:26,541
Cooperate with the investigation.

1739
01:33:28,416 --> 01:33:29,625
Don't touch them.

1740
01:33:29,708 --> 01:33:31,333
-Stop.
-Brother Chung.

1741
01:33:31,416 --> 01:33:33,416
What happened?

1742
01:33:33,500 --> 01:33:35,208
The women's choir is acting weird.

1743
01:33:35,875 --> 01:33:37,041
What's going on?

1744
01:33:37,625 --> 01:33:39,833
They said the choir was involved
in the theft.

1745
01:33:39,916 --> 01:33:41,541
The show might be canceled.

1746
01:33:43,416 --> 01:33:44,250
Chief--

1747
01:33:44,333 --> 01:33:46,125
-Where?
-In the restroom.

1748
01:33:55,208 --> 01:33:56,916
I'm in charge now.

1749
01:33:57,000 --> 01:33:58,958
Everyone out in the hall, line up.

1750
01:33:59,041 --> 01:34:00,041
Move.

1751
01:34:00,166 --> 01:34:01,416
Go.

1752
01:34:01,500 --> 01:34:03,500
-Hands on your head.
-Let's go first.

1753
01:34:03,583 --> 01:34:04,916
Hurry up.

1754
01:34:05,000 --> 01:34:06,750
Out. Move it.

1755
01:34:06,833 --> 01:34:08,166
-Let's go.
-Okay.

1756
01:34:08,875 --> 01:34:10,500
Not a sound.

1757
01:34:24,583 --> 01:34:27,500
A round of applause for

1758
01:34:27,583 --> 01:34:29,541
pianist Li Chien-Lun!

1759
01:34:29,625 --> 01:34:31,666
Everyone, excuse me.

1760
01:34:31,750 --> 01:34:33,458
There's a program change.

1761
01:34:33,583 --> 01:34:34,708
We have to

1762
01:34:34,791 --> 01:34:37,333
cancel the choir's performance.

1763
01:34:37,416 --> 01:34:38,375
But don't worry.

1764
01:34:38,458 --> 01:34:41,333
We'll bring on the next act right away.

1765
01:34:41,416 --> 01:34:45,000
Please welcome cellist Na Chi.

1766
01:34:45,083 --> 01:34:48,291
Enjoy the performance, and
let's give her a warm round of applause.

1767
01:34:48,375 --> 01:34:49,875
Excuse me.

1768
01:34:53,166 --> 01:34:54,333
Everyone, listen up.

1769
01:34:54,416 --> 01:34:55,291
Strip.

1770
01:34:55,375 --> 01:34:56,583
Full body search.

1771
01:34:56,666 --> 01:34:57,541
No way.

1772
01:34:57,625 --> 01:34:59,041
They still have rights.

1773
01:34:59,125 --> 01:35:00,625
You found nothing in here.

1774
01:35:00,708 --> 01:35:03,166
Human rights? For a bunch of inmates?

1775
01:35:03,750 --> 01:35:04,958
Strip, all of you.

1776
01:35:05,041 --> 01:35:06,666
Start the search.
Search.

1777
01:35:06,750 --> 01:35:08,041
Please cooperate.

1778
01:35:08,125 --> 01:35:10,041
Don't touch me. I'll undress myself.

1779
01:35:10,125 --> 01:35:10,958
Hurry up.

1780
01:35:12,166 --> 01:35:13,041
Search!

1781
01:35:14,541 --> 01:35:15,416
Please cooperate.

1782
01:35:15,500 --> 01:35:16,375
Search me!

1783
01:35:23,291 --> 01:35:24,458
Stand against the wall.

1784
01:35:25,750 --> 01:35:27,833
-Don't--
-Why won't you undress?

1785
01:35:27,916 --> 01:35:28,833
What?

1786
01:35:29,333 --> 01:35:31,125
-Please don't do this.
-Strip.

1787
01:35:31,208 --> 01:35:32,125
What are you doing?

1788
01:35:32,208 --> 01:35:33,375
-You.
-Why do this?

1789
01:35:33,458 --> 01:35:34,458
Why won't you strip?

1790
01:35:34,541 --> 01:35:36,416
I didn't steal anything. Why strip?

1791
01:35:36,500 --> 01:35:37,583
What?

1792
01:35:37,666 --> 01:35:39,083
Everyone, get dressed.

1793
01:35:39,916 --> 01:35:40,958
Get dressed.

1794
01:35:41,041 --> 01:35:42,083
Let my people go.

1795
01:35:42,166 --> 01:35:43,541
Let go.

1796
01:35:44,500 --> 01:35:46,166
-You.
-What?

1797
01:35:46,708 --> 01:35:48,166
The evidence of theft?

1798
01:35:48,250 --> 01:35:49,458
Show me.

1799
01:35:51,041 --> 01:35:52,916
So with no evidence,

1800
01:35:53,000 --> 01:35:55,333
you dragged them out,
slammed them to the wall

1801
01:35:55,416 --> 01:35:56,916
and forced them to strip?

1802
01:35:57,000 --> 01:35:59,625
Even if she were your wife,
show some respect.

1803
01:35:59,708 --> 01:36:01,125
What is this?

1804
01:36:01,208 --> 01:36:02,541
Are cops this sloppy?

1805
01:36:03,166 --> 01:36:06,500
Or because they're inmates,
you assume they stole it.

1806
01:36:06,583 --> 01:36:09,291
We didn't steal it.
We just went to the restroom.

1807
01:36:09,875 --> 01:36:11,708
I trust my people.

1808
01:36:11,791 --> 01:36:13,083
Calm down.

1809
01:36:13,166 --> 01:36:14,708
We're just following procedure.

1810
01:36:14,791 --> 01:36:16,708
-All right.
-Let me tell you.

1811
01:36:16,791 --> 01:36:18,916
If any one of them stole,

1812
01:36:19,000 --> 01:36:21,166
I'll take full responsibility.

1813
01:36:21,250 --> 01:36:23,041
But without sufficient evidence,

1814
01:36:23,125 --> 01:36:24,708
this is excessive force.

1815
01:36:24,791 --> 01:36:26,458
I'll have your badge taken away.

1816
01:36:26,541 --> 01:36:27,500
Excuse me.

1817
01:36:27,583 --> 01:36:29,791
We followed the book
during the investigation.

1818
01:36:29,875 --> 01:36:30,708
Sir.

1819
01:36:30,791 --> 01:36:31,875
We found the ring.

1820
01:36:31,958 --> 01:36:33,500
A girl picked it up.

1821
01:36:40,083 --> 01:36:41,791
All right, everyone, freeze.

1822
01:36:41,875 --> 01:36:43,375
-We're pulling out.
-Wait!

1823
01:36:44,500 --> 01:36:45,708
Pulling out?

1824
01:36:45,791 --> 01:36:47,416
You think this is a dump?

1825
01:36:47,500 --> 01:36:49,291
You think you can just walk away?

1826
01:36:51,000 --> 01:36:52,000
It's fine.

1827
01:36:52,916 --> 01:36:54,333
Everyone, get ready.

1828
01:36:54,875 --> 01:36:56,666
The Director-General is expecting us.

1829
01:36:56,750 --> 01:36:58,541
It's over.
Hurry and get ready.

1830
01:37:00,375 --> 01:37:01,291
It's fine now.

1831
01:37:14,500 --> 01:37:20,291
Applause for cellist Na Chi's
wonderful performance.

1832
01:37:20,916 --> 01:37:22,666
Weren't you all excited

1833
01:37:22,750 --> 01:37:25,125
about the Sunshine Women's Choir earlier?

1834
01:37:25,208 --> 01:37:26,791
Yes.

1835
01:37:26,875 --> 01:37:29,375
Here's some good news,

1836
01:37:29,458 --> 01:37:32,125
the Sunshine Women's Choir's show

1837
01:37:32,208 --> 01:37:34,500
will proceed as planned shortly.

1838
01:37:36,083 --> 01:37:38,375
Mom's going on stage.

1839
01:37:39,125 --> 01:37:41,833
Ten-minute break.

1840
01:37:46,041 --> 01:37:46,916
-So cute.
-Thanks.

1841
01:37:47,000 --> 01:37:49,541
You made this and didn't tell us
what it is.

1842
01:37:49,625 --> 01:37:52,833
This represents us:
the Sunshine Women's Choir.

1843
01:37:53,708 --> 01:37:55,375
-Where does it go?
-On your chest.

1844
01:37:58,583 --> 01:37:59,583
Nervous?

1845
01:38:03,916 --> 01:38:05,083
Don't be scared.

1846
01:38:05,958 --> 01:38:06,791
We're right here.

1847
01:38:13,041 --> 01:38:13,875
Just forget it.

1848
01:38:14,833 --> 01:38:15,916
Are you ready?

1849
01:38:16,000 --> 01:38:16,833
Ready.

1850
01:38:16,916 --> 01:38:18,750
You're the best.

1851
01:38:19,333 --> 01:38:20,875
Don't worry. You've got this.

1852
01:38:22,291 --> 01:38:24,458
Distinguished guests,
thank you for waiting.

1853
01:38:24,541 --> 01:38:27,541
Please welcome
the Sunshine Women's Choir

1854
01:38:27,625 --> 01:38:31,791
from the Northern Women's Prison
to the stage.

1855
01:38:48,458 --> 01:38:50,958
<i>Ten men</i>

1856
01:38:51,041 --> 01:38:55,333
<i>Seven are fools, eight are dull,</i>
<i>nine are bad</i>

1857
01:38:55,416 --> 01:38:58,625
<i>There's one everyone loves</i>

1858
01:38:58,708 --> 01:39:01,416
<i>Sisters, step out</i>

1859
01:39:01,500 --> 01:39:03,791
<i>Even if it's sweet talk</i>

1860
01:39:05,041 --> 01:39:07,458
{\an8}<i>Lure him over</i>

1861
01:39:07,541 --> 01:39:14,416
<i>Love him well. Don't let him leave again</i>

1862
01:39:22,583 --> 01:39:24,166
<i>Then be ready to fall</i>

1863
01:39:24,250 --> 01:39:25,875
<i>Falling, falling fast</i>

1864
01:39:26,541 --> 01:39:28,500
<i>If love is so great</i>

1865
01:39:28,583 --> 01:39:29,833
<i>So great, truly great</i>

1866
01:39:29,916 --> 01:39:32,333
<i>Why keep fighting it?</i>

1867
01:39:32,416 --> 01:39:34,666
<i>What's the point of struggling?</i>

1868
01:39:34,750 --> 01:39:36,791
<i>Am I worse than the rest?</i>

1869
01:39:38,333 --> 01:39:40,291
<i>Who's stuck home on weekends?</i>

1870
01:39:40,375 --> 01:39:42,333
<i>No one wants to stay home</i>

1871
01:39:42,416 --> 01:39:44,791
<i>Watching TV with popcorn</i>

1872
01:39:44,875 --> 01:39:46,458
<i>TV and popcorn</i>

1873
01:39:46,541 --> 01:39:48,416
<i>I think of the sweet words you said</i>

1874
01:39:49,041 --> 01:39:50,333
<i>Was it all a lie</i>

1875
01:39:50,416 --> 01:39:54,541
<i>Tears pouring down</i>

1876
01:39:54,625 --> 01:39:55,541
<i>Ten men</i>

1877
01:39:55,625 --> 01:39:58,291
<i>Seven are fools, eight are dull,</i>
<i>nine are bad</i>

1878
01:39:58,375 --> 01:40:00,083
<i>And there's one everyone loves</i>

1879
01:40:00,166 --> 01:40:02,708
<i>Sisters, step out.</i>

1880
01:40:02,791 --> 01:40:04,125
<i>Even if it's sweet talk</i>

1881
01:40:04,208 --> 01:40:05,875
<i>Lure him over</i>

1882
01:40:06,416 --> 01:40:10,791
<i>Love him well</i>
<i>Don't let him leave again</i>

1883
01:40:10,875 --> 01:40:12,041
<i>Ten men</i>

1884
01:40:12,125 --> 01:40:14,416
<i>Seven are fools, eight are dull,</i>
<i>nine are bad</i>

1885
01:40:14,500 --> 01:40:16,333
<i>And there's one everyone loves</i>

1886
01:40:16,416 --> 01:40:18,750
<i>Sisters, step out</i>

1887
01:40:18,833 --> 01:40:20,000
<i>Even if it's sweet talk</i>

1888
01:40:20,083 --> 01:40:21,375
<i>Lure him over</i>

1889
01:40:21,458 --> 01:40:28,000
<i>Love him well</i>
<i>Don't let him leave</i>

1890
01:40:30,375 --> 01:40:32,541
<i>One wrong step for money</i>
<i>I fell into the dark</i>

1891
01:40:32,625 --> 01:40:35,500
<i>No excuses, money, food</i>
<i>I risked my life for my kid</i>

1892
01:40:35,583 --> 01:40:36,875
<i>Listen to no one</i>

1893
01:40:36,958 --> 01:40:38,583
<i>Like I was possessed</i>

1894
01:40:39,541 --> 01:40:40,791
<i>Demon-possessed liar</i>

1895
01:40:40,875 --> 01:40:42,166
<i>For money, for gain</i>

1896
01:40:42,250 --> 01:40:44,041
<i>Fooling myself until I felt nothing</i>

1897
01:40:44,125 --> 01:40:45,125
<i>Fuckers like that</i>

1898
01:40:45,208 --> 01:40:46,916
<i>Lock 'em up to ward off evil</i>

1899
01:40:47,000 --> 01:40:49,041
<i>Gotta change fate</i>
<i>Change, change it up</i>

1900
01:40:49,125 --> 01:40:51,750
<i>Quit smoking, gambling</i>
<i>and fix your attitude</i>

1901
01:40:51,833 --> 01:40:55,333
<i>Change it all</i>
<i>Stop going mad for money</i>

1902
01:40:55,416 --> 01:40:58,666
<i>Now start fresh</i>
<i>Sisters, we fight together</i>

1903
01:40:58,750 --> 01:41:00,958
<i>Hold your ground</i>
<i>Don't pretend</i>

1904
01:41:01,041 --> 01:41:01,958
<i>No doubt</i>

1905
01:41:02,041 --> 01:41:03,666
<i>Listen, don't stray again</i>

1906
01:41:03,750 --> 01:41:05,541
<i>Sisters, fight together</i>

1907
01:41:05,625 --> 01:41:07,000
<i>Hang in there</i>

1908
01:41:07,083 --> 01:41:09,541
<i>Fear nothing, and we've got hope</i>

1909
01:41:09,625 --> 01:41:11,916
<i>Demons, get lost</i>
<i>Crazies, get lost</i>

1910
01:41:12,000 --> 01:41:14,333
<i>I'll deal with the fuckers</i>
<i>Get lost</i>

1911
01:41:19,583 --> 01:41:21,666
MOM, WE'LL BE GOOD AND WAIT FOR YOU.

1912
